node_modules/
coverage/
.env
.env.*
*.local
# The actual risk is a real secrets file landing in the repo — narrowed
# from `*credentials*`, which also matched (and would have silently
# dropped) this story's own legitimate src/credentials.ts and
# test/unit/credentials.test.ts. `*credentials*.json` keeps every .ts
# source file visible while still catching wyze-credentials.json,
# credentials-prod.json, credentials.json.bak, etc. — strictly more
# coverage than the literal name alone, at zero cost, and this repo is
# public. Real credentials never belong in this repo regardless of
# filename; this is a backstop, not a substitute for that rule.
*credentials*.json
*.log
